# Replication data. Data/Raw and Data/Processed are tracked, except the UN
# Comtrade bulk files: about 14 GB in total, 25 files exceed GitHub's 100 MB
# limit, and UN Comtrade terms restrict redistribution. They are re-downloaded
# with Python/comtrade_download.py; the catalogue and download log (with
# checksums) are tracked so the exact files can be identified. The two large
# US Census files are read from the authors' package, which is kept outside
# the repository (~/Downloads/GTW_replication); the last pattern is a backstop
# in case a copy is placed here again.
Replication Study/Data/Raw/Comtrade/**/*.gz
Replication Study/Data/Raw/Comtrade/**/*.part
Replication Study/Paper - Replication Package/

# Local checks of our rebuilt datasets against the authors' processed files.
# They need the full authors' package, so they are kept out of the repository.
Replication Study/Python/Checks/

# Secrets. API keys live in ~/.Renviron, outside the repository; these
# patterns are a backstop so a stray copy cannot be committed.
.Renviron
.env
*.secret
